{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time","id":1538853,"title":"Dealing with time","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-18T12:28:01-07:00","id":1538853,"title":"Dealing with time","content":"What metod of time travel do you use in your games?<br /> Multiple timelines? Fixed time? Changable time like in terminator?<br /> Personaly i prefer novicovs self consistency principle.<br /> You can go back in time but that means you where already back in time. Nothing will change. Only exeptions here are demons as creatures older than time they are not ruled by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:52:18-07:00","id":1538860,"title":"","content":"A combination of multiple timelines (what the Technocracy calls Everett Zones) and changeable time, with a Paradox-like effect that attempts (not always successfully) to punish the time traveler and to revert the timeline. Everett Zones are, in effect, Paradox Realms created by severe backlashes against temporal meddling; while less severe backlashes injure the time traveler or summon an equivalent of \u201cParadox Spirits\u201d to attempt to set the timeline back on its original course. It's <i>possible </i>to change the timeline; but doing so is <i>hard, </i>and carries serious consequences. <br /> <br /> The main difference between this and <i>actual </i>Paradox is that you don't need to work any Magick in order to generate temporal \u201cParadox\u201d; you simple need to be \u201cin the past\u201d and doing something disruptive. The Storyteller then determines how disruptive your action in the past is, and has you roll a pool based on that judgment call to determine how much \u201cTemporal Paradox\u201d you generate. <br /> <br /> It doesn't even matter how big the change is, if you're careful about it: you could make a <i>huge </i>change to the timeline, but in such a subtle way that it's not going to alter the history books; and that change will effectively be \u201cCoincidental\u201d, generating <i>no </i>\u201ctemporal Paradox\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T15:08:55-07:00","id":1538870,"title":"","content":"I wrote a whole thing about the options one can have for Time manipulation quite a number of years ago.<br /> <br /> The second page has the details for time travel<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222499-time-sphere-going-deeper\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222499-time-sphere-going-deeper\"> Time Sphere: Going Deeper - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222499-time-sphere-going-deeper\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222499-time-sphere-going-deeper </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I have always been in favour of the idea that different paradigms should inform in some ways how the spheres can be used, and whether certain effects are even possible given the assumptions certain paradigms bring with them. However, I never really liked the way HDYDT handled the idea, treating things more like a sphere tax rather than giving paradigms different uses of the spheres (I'm looking at you Chi Healing). So instead, I thought I'd go about stating how I would have ruled these kind of things, and what better way to start than to dive straight first into what is personally my favourite sphere, </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The long and short of it is that I would use whichever form of the timeline the mage themselves believes they are affecting. <br /> <br /> What I would add to this is that Paradox can be used to evoke a number of Time travel problem tropes, such as a flaw where for each point that backlashes, something changes in reality that only you notice, as far as everyone is concerned it has always been that way. This could be something trivial like the name of a town or something more drastic like the existence of someone's brother. A more drastic flaw, or perhaps a point from quiet would be that you keep being flashed back and forth between the two times, the one you visited and the one you came from. A variation of this is that you keep switching between alternative timelines, to the point at which you are not sure which one is the one you are actually in. A hobgoblin which would be interesting would be someone who has been disappeared in time due to a change you made, but you still hold them to exist. Another would be in the form of your own doppleganger from another time line, or perhaps you become the intruder from another timeline.<br /> <br /> And in place of a paradox realm, Being entirely unstuck from time, constantly being launched randomly from one time to another with little to no control as to when you end up.<br /> Speak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T06:39:56-07:00","id":1538899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time#post1538853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What metod of time travel do you use in your games?<br /> Multiple timelines? Fixed time? Changable time like in terminator?<br /> Personaly i prefer novicovs self consistency principle.<br /> You can go back in time but that means you where already back in time. Nothing will change. Only exeptions here are demons as creatures older than time they are not ruled by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the point of the game. A game based around time travel usually needs the possibility of temporal change to keep the stakes interesting. It allows for the goal of changing history, or the need to avoid changing history. That said, I suppose you could have a good action style game where no changes in time will stick, the main goal of time travel is information, and the enemies will stop at nothing to avoid the heroes getting back with the vital intelligence that will win the modern war.<br /> <br /> One of the ideas I like is temporal convergence, where not only can multiple timelines proceed out of a single point, but multiple timelines can proceed into a single point. To put it another way, there can be more than one past someone travels into by going back in time. It would give a good platform for a Temporal War as each side fights to reinforce their own past and thus their own strength in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T20:50:55-07:00","id":1539183,"title":"","content":"It's not really come up in any of my games, so it'd probably depend. I admit though, I tend to like the idea of allowing the characters to change the past, if only because there are a lot of ways to have it backfire on them if/when they return to the future. It's a fun way to explore hubris and consequences (and maybe make a few long term continuity changes for things that might have happened in the past: returning enemies, new spouses/children, and so on.)<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of alternate timelines, but I'm not really sure how I'd incorporate that. It's fun to contemplate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T02:41:54-07:00","id":1539191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539183#post1539183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not really come up in any of my games, so it'd probably depend. I admit though, I tend to like the idea of allowing the characters to change the past, if only because there are a lot of ways to have it backfire on them if/when they return to the future. It's a fun way to explore hubris and consequences (and maybe make a few long term continuity changes for things that might have happened in the past: returning enemies, new spouses/children, and so on.)<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of alternate timelines, but I'm not really sure how I'd incorporate that. It's fun to contemplate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an etherite rote for traveling to alternative versions of the past using Time, Corr and Entropy<br /> <br /> and I believe there is a void engineer rote that uses different ranks of these spheres to travel to alternate universes which they call \u2018everette volumes\u2019<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T07:10:47-07:00","id":1539205,"title":"","content":"Mind 4/Time 3 for a mage to project their mind into someone in the past and act through their body, psuedo-quantum leap style. I say psuedo because as I recall Sam was actually physically back in the past and everyone else just saw and heard the original person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T12:16:55-07:00","id":1539381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539205#post1539205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind 4/Time 3 for a mage to project their mind into someone in the past and act through their body, psuedo-quantum leap style. I say psuedo because as I recall Sam was actually physically back in the past and everyone else just saw and heard the original person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Time 3 just a few seconds (turns) of rewinding time?<br /> <br /> I don't think you can reach far in the past with Time 3, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> Now, about the &quot;alternative universes&quot;, that is not a line I favor too much, because it is meaningless for the game world, since whatever changes you enact &quot;there&quot; won't affect anything down &quot;here&quot;, unless you're bringing something vital or precious from &quot;there&quot; to &quot;here&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for simply traveling to the past, unless you can't actually affect the present by altering it (no matter the consequences), it is also useless - as in, it serves no purpose for the narrative.<br /> <br /> So, my take is:<br /> <br /> You travel to the Past, you enact changes in the Present.<br /> <br /> This however, as anybody with a minimum of common sense can realize, is absolutely shaboinky for any story and would quickly turn narrating games into a nightmare.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the way I deal with it is with what I call as &quot;Time Ripples&quot;<br /> <br /> So, instead of treating Time simultaneously (Past, Present and Future happens all at the same time), I give it a sort of &quot;delay&quot;, upon which it actually takes some time for the changes in the temporal continuum to fully manifest, and those changes come gradually in the form of &quot;waves&quot;, rather than an instantaneous alteration.<br /> <br /> It's as if time is a pool of water, and when you throw a stone into the Past, it creates waves of temporal alterations through it.<br /> <br /> Let's talk about the Future for a while so that I may explain. Now, let us imagine that, in the future, there's WW3 between NATO and the Brics.<br /> <br /> The world is devastated in nuclear Armageddon, but the Brics nations &quot;win&quot; (interpret this &quot;victory&quot; as you wish)<br /> <br /> This is seen in a vision by an Oracle in the PRESENT. Desperate to avoid such outcome and because the visions aren't precise, he decides to step forward into the Future to learn what causes this catastrophe. There, he learns that a chain of events caused by the assassination of the president Kennedy - not the old Kennedy, the modern one, elected president of the US in 2028, and assassinated in 2030, will end up leading to WW3.<br /> <br /> Now (2024), our Oracle finds out that he has 6 years to save the world.<br /> <br /> And he does. By 2029 he reveals the secret CIA conspiracy that plotted the assassination of yet another Kennedy, and doom is avoided.<br /> <br /> Or is it thou?<br /> <br /> Well, meanwhile in the future, the temporal ripples begin to be unleashed. Reality begin to be distorted by the ripples. Some history books rotting at the wastelands of Washington DC no longer tell about RFK assassination in 2030, but rather about his two mandates as president and how he finally signed the agreements with the Russian oligarchs that deposed Putin. Some weeks later, the city of Chicago reapers, intact. A few moments afterwards, the Kremlin stands intact in the middle of Moscow's wasteland. Then the forbidden city reappears in the wastelands of Beinjing. And so on, so forth.<br /> <br /> To the sleepers, they are absolutely incapable to perceive those changes; they don't even notice it. If one asks the sleepers, they'll often offer conflicting tales about the chronology of history and about the perceptions of things in the Present.<br /> <br /> For the awaken thou, all these changes are immediately spotten. Not only that, the awaken will start to develop a DUAL MEMORY of the Past; they'll know how history went in the &quot;formal&quot; way, but they'll also be aware of the &quot;alternative history&quot; unfolding.<br /> <br /> Now, back to our story: what happens is that, a group of Sino-Soviet mages consider this divergence as unacceptable, because despite of all the calamity, the final outcome was deemed as &quot;net positive&quot; for the forces of the &quot;New Axis&quot;.<br /> <br /> They then identify the point of distortion, from which the time ripples emanate, as being in 2029 when the CIA conspiracy plot was averted, and decide to go back in time and rectify this situation.<br /> <br /> So, now our heroic oracle (I'm sorry, I forgot that &quot;Oracle&quot; in Mage are the demigods Mages that reach Ascension. What I mean here is an &quot;oracle&quot; with lower case &quot;o&quot; - aka someone that sees the future) has to contend with a bunch of really angry fascist Eastern Mages hellbent on stopping him.<br /> <br /> <br /> For this types of stories, it is always good to put a time frame upon which afterwards the temporal ripples finally cease and the temporal continuum gets stabilized and solid.<br /> <br /> In the case above, let's say that the &quot;Cabal of the New Axis&quot; from the future only have 6 months to undo the changes.<br /> <br /> After that time, the ripples finally cease, and they'll begin to cease to exist in the Present, until disappearing completely. And their future versions will no longer know the two alternative versions of history, and they'll never know they even went to the &quot;Past&quot; (their Past, our Present). In fact, after those 6 months, THEY HAVEN'T. If they fail to stop the oracle in 6 months, the only person in the world that will know of that alternative future will be our heroic oracle, and that Future (which was once certain) would forever remain as just an alternative Future that never came to pass.<br /> <br /> The same holds true for traveling to the Past.<br /> <br /> Doing that also prevents idiots trying to assassinate baby Hitler (or teaching teen Hitler how to be a good painter) every single weekend. Changes too big (like removing Hitler from history) send Time Ripples so large that EVERY AWAKENED in the world - and across multiple timelines! - can easily spot.<br /> <br /> That's almost guaranteed to send the Technocracy, or the Traditions or BOTH against the baby fool that attempts such stupidity.<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, if someone gets back in time to murder baby-you, you'll get in that &quot;quantum-state&quot; where you're both &quot;dead and alive&quot; for some time while the ripples are dispersed, giving you time to get back in time to prevent your own murder as a baby.<br /> <br /> Because of that, small changes in the past are easier to achieve. If your girlfriend gets assassinated in your remote wooden shackle and you get there when the murder just finished the deed, so you kill the murder and decides to go 1 day back in time to kill the murder before he does it, nobody will ever know that this small change has ever been enacted (unless there was some Mage using Time 1 at the place where the time travel was used in either way, and that would've been quite the coincidence to happen).<br /> <br /> Killing baby Hitler or Baby Napoleon or stepping in a butterfly in the Jurassic period however would be immediately perceived by every mage in the entire world (and in the case of the Jurassic butterfly you'd end up having time travellers being summoned to prevent this from the pre historic times to Mages living in the Galactic Empire)<br /> <br /> What's more, the time Traveller is always immune to &quot;Time Stabilization&quot;. Back to the example of the &quot;New Axis Cabal&quot;. 6 months after they fail in their mission, the heroic oracle is the only one in the world that knows about the alternative future and about the ravenous Mages from that alternative future that failed to stop him. To the rest of the world, those guys never existed. But the hero remains them, because he is now a &quot;time anomaly&quot;, because he now exists in the Present and in an alternative Future that never came to be.<br /> <br /> What do we do with these &quot;time anomalies&quot;? Well, that's up to you guys as STs. Maybe nothing, the time traveller hero's life keeps going normally but he has a very interesting &quot;science fiction&quot; history about alt-history to tell his friends.<br /> <br /> Or, if you're feeling particularly sadistic, maybe he could be visited by some interesting paradox-spirits next time he suffers a backlash... Maybe the &quot;New Axis Cabal&quot; comes to torment him but not as the &quot;ghosts&quot; of future Mages that don't exist, but rather as vengeful Paradox Spirits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T14:42:09-07:00","id":1539498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539381#post1539381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Time 3 just a few seconds (turns) of rewinding time?<br /> <br /> I don't think you can reach far in the past with Time 3, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a rewinding time effect. Time 3 allows a mage to cast spells across time. The wording is funky but it is there. If a mage wanted to read the mind of someone in the past that would be Mind 3/Time 3. Mind 4/Time 3 would allow the mage to mind control/puppet someone in the past or possibly even project into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-30T18:18:21-07:00","id":1539565,"title":"","content":"I find that many time-altering actions would create Paradox loops that would expel the time-traveler (or negate their existence), like shooting your kid self. In a way that no one remember your action in the past, but your kind of stuck in this loop, unless someone helps you out. So keeping out of these loops is paramount. <br /> <br /> So not everybody can effect the past, I would say, and even what they can affect is limited. The Paradox for changing world-events would decimate any under 5+ Arete Mage (and who knows further). I think there should be some good things you can change, but not that much, otherwise mages would be doing that stuff all the time. And they don't. Hell, even the Cult of Ecstasy, who are Time mages, are more Mind and Life than Time-users.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think it should be one thing very well thought out. A chronicle can't 'just have that'. It must be about it, if it has. (Of course, to each game it's own)<br /> If indeed there was world-event possibility for Time-magic, I would say yeah... while I don't like it, better to say that the mages responsible create a new timeline for them. Good for them, yeah, but they are gone from their original one. And depending if you consider there to be a 'true timeline' root, than theirs might just crumble with time...<br /> <br /> And hell yeah, people and places that &quot;shouldn't exist&quot; would still be alive, just gradually 'noticing' they aren't true anymore. And they are paradox generators around them, Marauder- bound if they are mages... That is the sort of thing I find cool. You weaken you enemy by killing them in the past, but they might yet fight back! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T22:46:57-07:00","id":1539621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539565#post1539565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that many time-altering actions would create Paradox loops that would expel the time-traveler (or negate their existence), like shooting your kid self. In a way that no one remember your action in the past, but your kind of stuck in this loop, unless someone helps you out. So keeping out of these loops is paramount.<br /> <br /> So not everybody can effect the past, I would say, and even what they can affect is limited. The Paradox for changing world-events would decimate any under 5+ Arete Mage (and who knows further). I think there should be some good things you can change, but not that much, otherwise mages would be doing that stuff all the time. And they don't. Hell, even the Cult of Ecstasy, who are Time mages, are more Mind and Life than Time-users.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think it should be one thing very well thought out. A chronicle can't 'just have that'. It must be about it, if it has. (Of course, to each game it's own)<br /> If indeed there was world-event possibility for Time-magic, I would say yeah... while I don't like it, better to say that the mages responsible create a new timeline for them. Good for them, yeah, but they are gone from their original one. And depending if you consider there to be a 'true timeline' root, than theirs might just crumble with time...<br /> <br /> And hell yeah, people and places that &quot;shouldn't exist&quot; would still be alive, just gradually 'noticing' they aren't true anymore. And they are paradox generators around them, Marauder- bound if they are mages... That is the sort of thing I find cool. You weaken you enemy by killing them in the past, but they might yet fight back!</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely hate this notion of &quot;oh yes, you can totally travel to the Past... But then Paradox will unmake you and nothing at all will change&quot;.<br /> <br /> The reason why I like &quot;time waves&quot; is because it actually allows people to do it, but the constraints onto &quot;why don't Mages do it all the Time&quot; aren't that &quot;nobody will know you have ever existed because Paradox will erase your entire existence from the timeline&quot;. But rather that the stupid Mage number 231 that tried to assassinate Hitler found out that the Technocracy is pretty adamant in their zeal about &quot;time continuity&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or maybe even that's a subject that is particularly dear to several groups of Nephandi who always rush to the rescue of dear Adolph.<br /> <br /> Or, if you wanna be extra crazy, the moment you try to shoot a certain Austrian painter, a group from the year 3127 which are NOT the Technocrats shows up to stop you, claiming that no matter how awful WW2 was, but it is essential to the future, because it sets a chain of events that result in the end of the Technocracy and Traditions and the creation of their group that turned the world into an utopia.<br /> <br /> Now, for lesser events, it should be entirely possible. And the &quot;time waves&quot; would be far smaller, so it is unlikely that you as the Narrator would feel the need to summon the Khlathius Empire from the year 40.000 to bash the offending Mage in the head (but do keep that option open if someone is stupid enough to try to kill baby Alexander the Great or baby Caesar, baby Einstein, baby Tutankhamen and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T22:50:47-07:00","id":1539622,"title":"","content":"I also like to deal with paradoxes (not the game Paradox with capital &quot;P&quot;, but the real time paradox). What happens if you go back in time and kill your own grandfather while he's still just a teenager?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T04:45:11-07:00","id":1539631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539498#post1539498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This isn't a rewinding time effect. Time 3 allows a mage to cast spells across time. The wording is funky but it is there. If a mage wanted to read the mind of someone in the past that would be Mind 3/Time 3. Mind 4/Time 3 would allow the mage to mind control/puppet someone in the past or possibly even project into them.</div> </div> </div> </div>you\u2019re going to have to source that one. I do not believe this has ever been the case<br /> <br /> unless you are referring exclusively to sensory magic, that I would agree with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T07:11:20-07:00","id":1539634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539631#post1539631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> you\u2019re going to have to source that one. I do not believe this has ever been the case<br /> <br /> unless you are referring exclusively to sensory magic, that I would agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 20th, Page 523, Time 3 Section, Emphasis mine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combining this Rank with other Spheres, the mage can affect other Patterns (Forces, Life, or Matter 2), <b>cast Effects across distance and time (Correspondence 3)</b>, move back in time while recalling events from the future she just left (Life 3/Mind 1), or even invoke multiple probabilities (Entropy 3). <b>Again, such attempts are Paradox magnets with awful longterm consequences.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence can only be handling the distance part of the effect, so Time 3 has to the be the one covering time. This also can't be limited to sensory effects alone because those are already covered by Time 2's Past and Future Sight. It can't mean moving things from one time period to another, since that is clearly covered by Time 5. However, casting effects across Time appears to be the province of Time 3.<br /> <br /> Now, that first sentence is not going to win any awards, and there is a case to be made that parts of it were editing mistakes. However, that clause is the clearest written of the four. Also the second sentence implies that some of those effects were meant to be the kind of thing that use the special UberParadox rules for altering the past.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T07:47:37-07:00","id":1539638,"title":"","content":"Personally, I prefer to enable as many different notions of how messing with time can work as possible, rather than settling on just one. To this end, I'm considering a notion of <i>timepoints</i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b, where the nature of the timepoint determines which set of temporal mechanics are in effect. <br /> <br /> By default, a timepoint is <i>fluid</i>, and the event in question can be changed easily. If you create a temporal inconsistency (such as killing your father before he meets your mother), then history now has an inconsistency in it. History doesn't try to correct the inconsistency, though the time traveler may face consequences akin to a Paradox Backlash for having created the inconsistency. <br /> <br /> But there are three other types of timepoints: <br /> <br /> A <i>Static timepoint</i> resists changes. If you try to create an inconsistency, chance events will conspire to prevent you from doing so; and if you succeed anyway, further events will conspire to contain and mitigate the consequences. Eventually, the original timeline will be restored. <br /> <br /> A <i>Dynamic timepoint</i> is a lot like a fluid timepoint, except that when you create an inconsistency, it gets shunted off into an alternate timeline. Individual timelines when examined in isolation can contain inconsistencies; but the larger multiverse of timelines when viewed as a whole remains consistent. Dynamic timepoints are also sometimes called <i>decision points</i>, because even without Time travelers meddling with them they tend to \u201csplit the the timeline\u201d based on what people involved in the event decide to do. <br /> <br /> An <i>Entropic timepoint</i> is one where time meddling is discouraged by an extreme version of the Butterfly Effect: creating an inconsistency <i>here </i>works exactly <i>opposite</i> of creating an inconsistency in a Static timepoint, as the timeline essentially shatters and entirely unpredictable changes spiral out of control. An example of this can be found in the 2011 <i>Flash Comics</i> event called \u201cFlashpoint\u201d: Barry Allen attempted to go back in time and prevent his mother's death, and succeeded; but when he returned to the present, Aquaman and the Atlanteans were at war with Wonder Woman and the Amazons, much of Europe was submerged, Bruce Wayne was replaced by his father as the Batman after the mugger shot Bruce instead of his parents, and \u201cthe Superman\u201d was being kept in a vault after government agents had found his spacecraft when he first arrived in Earth. <br /> <br /> Time Magick lets you identify which type of timepoint a particular event is. It lets you trace a chain of events forward or back from a particular event, letting you identify future or past events that are causally connected to the current event; and with sufficient ranks in Time, you can even travel to them. When departing from a Dynamic timepoint, you can control which timeline you travel along. Near the upper ranks of Time, you can even mess with <i>what type of timepoint</i> a particular event is, letting you affix an event in history by making it Static, shifting it to a Dynamic timepoint that splits the timeline whenever you mess with it, or poisoning the event with Entropy so that messing with it blows up in the face of the meddler. With effort, you can also restore the timepoint to its default fluid status, removing the added consequences involved in messing with it. <br /> <br /> Again, <b>Mage</b> shouldn't lock itself into one way of handling time travel hijinks; it should provide a framework that enables whichever approaches the Storyteller wants to use. If you like history to be unchangeable, lean heavily on Static timepoints; of you like the notion of a multiverse, lean heavily on Dynamic timepoints; if you're enthralled with the Butterfly Effect, lean heavily on Entropic timepoints. If you just want to keep things simple, stick to fluid timepoints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T16:09:09-07:00","id":1539667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539634#post1539634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure thing:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Correspondence can only be handling the distance part of the effect, so Time 3 has to the be the one covering time. This also can't be limited to sensory effects alone because those are already covered by Time 2's Past and Future Sight. It can't mean moving things from one time period to another, since that is clearly covered by Time 5. However, casting effects across Time appears to be the province of Time 3.<br /> <br /> Now, that first sentence is not going to win any awards, and there is a case to be made that parts of it were editing mistakes. However, that clause is the clearest written of the four. Also the second sentence implies that some of those effects were meant to be the kind of thing that use the special UberParadox rules for altering the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes more sense that it would allow you to cast Time loops from a distance, causing bubbles of time to reverse in areas you are nowhere near. Such a thing is in line with how Time 3 is said to work across M20, and would also invoke paradox in the same way as standard time loops, which then fits this second line you have emphasized. <br /> <br /> Considering that Time 4 triggers are essentially casting magic in to the future, to allow such a thing with Time 3 would render this rather major aspects of Time 4 entirely redundant, so it is highly unlikely your interpretation it the intended one. Especially considering the lack of any other supporting material for such an interpretation.<br /> <br /> As I see it, casting effects backwards in time would only be possible at Time 4 at minimum, but better done at Time 5.<br /> <br /> For Time 4, I would see it as essentially creating a time trigger effect, locking it in to an object or person, and then sending that backwards in time using Prime to not undo the effect (the same way Mind is used to exclude your memories when reversing yourself).<br /> <br /> While Time 5 allows you to actually throw magic back in time.<br /> <br /> You could do a similar thing with Time 3 only in one respect. Creating a trinket and reversing time but either excluding the trinket (so the locked in effect is active at an earlier point) or reverse the trinket itself (with Prime to exclude the reversal of locking the effect in to the object) such that where the object was back when you reversed it to, it is now a trinket at that point in the timeline, whatever that means depends on what you made your locked effect do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T18:27:18-07:00","id":1539670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539667#post1539667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes more sense that it would allow you to cast Time loops from a distance, causing bubbles of time to reverse in areas you are nowhere near. Such a thing is in line with how Time 3 is said to work across M20, and would also invoke paradox in the same way as standard time loops, which then fits this second line you have emphasized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you can interpret it that way if you want. For my money, though, casting time loops at a distance is in no way casting an Effect across time. Space, yes, but not time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering that Time 4 triggers are essentially casting magic in to the future, to allow such a thing with Time 3 would render this rather major aspects of Time 4 entirely redundant, so it is highly unlikely your interpretation it the intended one. Especially considering the lack of any other supporting material for such an interpretation. </div> </div> </div>Time triggers are still way more useful than scouting out a possible future, casting an effect into it, and hoping it\u2019s the one that ends up happening. You still need Time 4 for the real deal.<br /> <br /> I do think casting into the past get overpowered quite quickly, but it is also subject to UberParadox just like full time travel. That\u2019s the mechanic that\u2019s supposed to keep time shenanigans at bay, after all. Also, Time 3 doesn\u2019t grant Time Immunity. In a game where that matters altering the past before Time 5 is a very dangerous proposition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T00:24:41-07:00","id":1539681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539670#post1539670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you can interpret it that way if you want. For my money, though, casting time loops at a distance is in no way casting an Effect across time. Space, yes, but not time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Time triggers are still way more useful than scouting out a possible future, casting an effect into it, and hoping it\u2019s the one that ends up happening. You still need Time 4 for the real deal.<br /> <br /> I do think casting into the past get overpowered quite quickly, but it is also subject to UberParadox just like full time travel. That\u2019s the mechanic that\u2019s supposed to keep time shenanigans at bay, after all. Also, Time 3 doesn\u2019t grant Time Immunity. In a game where that matters altering the past before Time 5 is a very dangerous proposition.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>ok, let\u2019s hear how you organise the mechanics of this. Because as it stands, this interpretation means you can use Time 3 to cast an effect 5 weeks in to the future in a manner that mimics what Time 4 can do, or the past in a manner that Time 4 cannot based on nothing more than the words you have quoted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T06:46:09-07:00","id":1539690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539681#post1539681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ok, let\u2019s hear how you organise the mechanics of this. Because as it stands, this interpretation means you can use Time 3 to cast an effect 5 weeks in to the future in a manner that mimics what Time 4 can do, or the past in a manner that Time 4 cannot based on nothing more than the words you have quoted.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, its like looking into the future. The mage sees <i>a</i> future, but there is no guarantee it is the future that comes to pass. Time 3 lets the mage cast into <b>a specific</b> future, but it isn't necessarily the future that will come to pass. She could cast a fireball on Bartholomew Wombat, gentleman thief, when he shows up to steal the crown jewels at midnight on April 8th, but if Lord Wombat shows up at a different time, or a different day, or to steal something else, etc... well the spell doesn't show up because she didn't cast it into that timeline. There's no ability to tailor the Time 3 version to a variety of different events and no ability to make the spell go off at a set time regardless of events. All of that is Time 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if a mage wants to cast a spell that goes off in 5 weeks, that's Time 4. Time 3 only lets him cast into a specific future that he's pre-cog'd, and the spell only shows up if the future he foresaw does. It's honestly of limited utility when it comes to future events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T07:34:21-07:00","id":1539691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539690#post1539690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, its like looking into the future. The mage sees <i>a</i> future, but there is no guarantee it is the future that comes to pass. Time 3 lets the mage cast into <b>a specific</b> future, but it isn't necessarily the future that will come to pass. She could cast a fireball on Bartholomew Wombat, gentleman thief, when he shows up to steal the crown jewels at midnight on April 8th, but if Lord Wombat shows up at a different time, or a different day, or to steal something else, etc... well the spell doesn't show up because she didn't cast it into that timeline. There's no ability to tailor the Time 3 version to a variety of different events and no ability to make the spell go off at a set time regardless of events. All of that is Time 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> So if a mage wants to cast a spell that goes off in 5 weeks, that's Time 4. Time 3 only lets him cast into a specific future that he's pre-cog'd, and the spell only shows up if the future he foresaw does. It's honestly of limited utility when it comes to future events.</div> </div> </div> </div>That renders the effect a bit\u2026.unusable, as one could argue the act of casting an effect in to the future is enough to change the direction you take to the future you are to see. If you imagine how many decisions people make are based on random occurrences, going to a coffeeshop because the light caught its window just right to hit your eye and notice it, taking a left down the road because you heard a dog barking and was curious what was there.<br /> <br /> all these little things can make a single day play out in thousands of different possible permutations. Add on to that the compounded chaos that comes from remembering literally every human is capable of makes decisions differently from equally random circumstances, and said decisions then impact other\u2019s decisions, you get situations where depending on whether you chose green sock or blue socks in the morning, you might end up with a new friend that is the beginning of a relationship, or getting caught up in a car crash that sets you back 10 years.<br /> <br /> Simply knowing the future is enough to change it by some\u2019s metrics. I would be hardpressed to consider where one could actually draw the line for this effect being of any use in such a chaotic environment.<br /> <br /> if you wished to make one\u2019s magic follow one\u2019s understanding of time, then you are left with the question of what to do for one who believes time is an arrow, constant, persistent, and immutable. That if they see the future then that future *will* happen, and anything they do will simply contribute towards said future happening.<br /> and that leads to your intepretation of Time 3 being essentially Time 4","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T07:56:28-07:00","id":1539694,"title":"","content":"Precognition is equivalent to time travel into the past in the important ways, in that it involves <i>something </i>going backwards in time (information, in the case of foresight) and potentially leading to time paradoxes. See my previous post as to how I'd resolve those paradoxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T08:22:29-07:00","id":1539696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539691#post1539691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That renders the effect a bit\u2026.unusable, as one could argue the act of casting an effect in to the future is enough to change the direction you take to the future you are to see. If you imagine how many decisions people make are based on random occurrences, going to a coffeeshop because the light caught its window just right to hit your eye and notice it, taking a left down the road because you heard a dog barking and was curious what was there.<br /> <br /> all these little things can make a single day play out in thousands of different possible permutations. Add on to that the compounded chaos that comes from remembering literally every human is capable of makes decisions differently from equally random circumstances, and said decisions then impact other\u2019s decisions, you get situations where depending on whether you chose green sock or blue socks in the morning, you might end up with a new friend that is the beginning of a relationship, or getting caught up in a car crash that sets you back 10 years.<br /> <br /> Simply knowing the future is enough to change it by some\u2019s metrics. I would be hardpressed to consider where one could actually draw the line for this effect being of any use in such a chaotic environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. That's why I'm not worried about Time 3 encroaching on one of Time 4's key abilities. Even if we are significantly more generous than you just described, there still aren't great odds of the spell showing up.<br /> <br /> That's not to say casting directly into the future has no use, but it works better for fact finding. The mage could use Mind to figure out what Lord Wombat is thinking in a future where he tries to steal the crown jewels, or cast a spell on a magical security system to see how it might react. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you wished to make one\u2019s magic follow one\u2019s understanding of time, then you are left with the question of what to do for one who believes time is an arrow, constant, persistent, and immutable. That if they see the future then that future *will* happen, and anything they do will simply contribute towards said future happening.<br /> and that leads to your intepretation of Time 3 being essentially Time 4 </div> </div> </div>Well since Mage tends to talk in terms of possible futures, its not something I really considered. To tell the truth I don't know how I would handle having the future be set in stone for one mage and constantly shifting for another. I don't really see a way of preserving both at the same time. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T08:47:08-07:00","id":1539699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539696#post1539696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well since Mage tends to talk in terms of possible futures, its not something I really considered. To tell the truth I don't know how I would handle having the future be set in stone for one mage and constantly shifting for another. I don't really see a way of preserving both at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Whether a timepoint is Static, Dynamic, Entropic, or simply fluid shouldn't depend on a particular mage's Focus. How the mage <i>deals</i> with the timepoint can and should depend on his Focus; but what he's dealing with shouldn't. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T09:50:12-07:00","id":1539706,"title":"","content":"Hmm i always thought time 3 is only for slowing/speeding up things. Time 4 was for trigger magic and time stop and time 5 for time travel","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T15:22:51-07:00","id":1539722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539621#post1539621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I absolutely hate this notion of &quot;oh yes, you can totally travel to the Past... But then Paradox will unmake you and nothing at all will change&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, i'm with you on that, I never said Paradox should unmake. Paradox is backlash against the action being made in the first place, but it affects people and place around. So... the action should be made, the change should occur.<br /> <br /> Just trying to present a situation where there is possibility of change, without being so fluid and easy that we wonder 'hey, why aren't we stopping X tragedy&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T16:24:10-07:00","id":1539806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1538853-dealing-with-time?p=1539696#post1539696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well since Mage tends to talk in terms of possible futures, its not something I really considered. To tell the truth I don't know how I would handle having the future be set in stone for one mage and constantly shifting for another. I don't really see a way of preserving both at the same time.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Alternative realities is the only answer to that. <br /> <br /> But then, so too would the Past be mutable... And there's actually just one constant &quot;Observed Present&quot; where the quantum wave is collapsed... Everything else, Past and Future, exist in states of juxtaposition.<br /> <br /> There would be, therefore, a past upon which Hitler became a famous Austrian painter, and perhaps an even darker present - for example, WW2 is fought as a much quicker war against the Soviet Union, after which Communism is demonized but the Fascist ideology spreads throughout the world, even in the UK and US, so there's no Cold War, but rather a fascist &quot;American Imperium&quot; that simply dethrones all other old Empires in the world. Maybe even with an alliance between Japan and USSR during WW2.<br /> <br /> In Italy, Mussolini Jr is a puppet of the Americans (the old Mussi sides with the allies).<br /> <br /> Or perhaps there is a Cold War yes, but between the Empires - UK, France and US, all of which are fascists.<br /> <br /> Then in another reality, the Technocratic Union of Reptiles wage a secret war against the Reptile Mages of the Traditions, because 65 millions of years ago a certain meteor shocked against Luna instead of Terra, and thus the only mammals on the planet are the pests that the &quot;Reptiles sapiens&quot; call as &quot;rats&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, this means that some Mages could look up into many alternative realities and see a range of possibilities, while others would see a single arrow, all according to Paradigm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}